n {:value ""} "Beach Volleyball in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/VBV'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Beach Volleyball at the 2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "6 – 18 August 2016"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "2"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/922"} "Arena Copacabana, Copacabana, Rio de Janeiro"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "If the backdrop of Buckingham Palace and the Palace of Westminster for the 2012 beach volleyball tournament in London were impressive, then the venue for the 2016 tournament was equally impressive, which was played in the 12,000-seater purpose built arena on the Copacabana Beach, with the famous Sugar Loaf Mountain in the background. This was only the second time, after Bondi Beach in 2000, that the beach volleyball competition has been played on a natural beach."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Although the sport’s roots are in the USA, beach volleyball is as synonymous with Brazil as much as football, and any talk of beach volleyball in Brazil leads inevitably to mention of the Copacabana Beach, along which there is row-upon-row of volleyball courts in regular use by Rio residents. Despite its pedigree, however, and being the leading Olympic beach volleyball medallists with 11, Brazil had won just two golds prior to the Rio Games, in 1996 (women) and 2004 (men). Being on home sand, and having the reigning men’s and women’s world champions in their squads, Brazil looked like rectifying that situation. The women certainly went into the competition confident of gold as they occupied all three medal places at the 2015 World Championship in the Netherlands."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Matches were played to the best-of-three-sets amidst music and revelry. The first team to win 21 points (with at least a two-point margin) won the set. That applied to the first two sets only, if a third deciding set was needed, then it was the first to 15 – again with a minimum of a two-point margin. Seven countries made their début in Rio: Chile, Qatar and Tunisia in the men’s events and Costa Rica, Egypt and Venezuela in the women’s events while Poland qualified for both men’s and women’s tournaments for the first time."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Surprisingly, despite the high expectations placed upon them, Brazil had only two finalists, one in each of the men’s and women’s tournament and they won just one title, the men’s, thanks to " [:a {:href "/athletes/122888"} "Alison Cerutti"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/132791"} "Bruno Schmidt"] ". America’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/94592"} "Kerri Walsh Jennings"] " was going for her fourth consecutive gold but had to settle for bronze. Germany won its first beach volleyball gold medal courtesy of " [:a {:href "/athletes/112500"} "Laura Ludwig"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/130339"} "Kira Walkenhorst"] " while " [:a {:href "/athletes/123456"} "Daniele Lupo"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/123455"} "Paolo Nicolai"] "’s men’s silver medal was Italy’s first ever medal in the sport. Brazil with one gold and one silver was the only nation to win more than one medal in Rio."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:t